            [
                'id' => 3,
                'title' => "Rebuild Annual Rollovers",
                'slug' => "rebuild-annual-rollovers",
                'content' => "<h1 id=\"when-do-you-need-to-rebuild-annual-rollovers\">When do you need to Rebuild Annual Rollovers?</h1><ul><li><p>When an accounting adjustment is posted after a financial year is rolled over, it will cause an imbalance in the subsequent year’s balance sheet.</p></li><li><p>The imbalance can be captured in 2.1 of final financial reporting workpaper in the subsequent year</p></li><li><p>Example:</p></li></ul><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/YDYN9Pbvjo6zvJvvEoGOfovFjgjmtyEydIFgAhG1.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/YDYN9Pbvjo6zvJvvEoGOfovFjgjmtyEydIFgAhG1.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"how-to-rebuild-annual-rollovers\">How to Rebuild Annual Rollovers?</h1><ul><li><p>Accounting &gt;&gt; Adjustments &gt;&gt; Rebuild Annual Rollovers &gt;&gt; OK &gt;&gt; Wait for normally 1-2 minutes &gt;&gt; OK</p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/psHn1Rzf0kuPHN0Gq2hEIKpJl5yCVUnHBpPca6qP.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/psHn1Rzf0kuPHN0Gq2hEIKpJl5yCVUnHBpPca6qP.png\"></p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/s85zeykBPV6poWFpRZ18c0SjXjK0b5XvEOvYbVXe.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/s85zeykBPV6poWFpRZ18c0SjXjK0b5XvEOvYbVXe.png\"></p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/aDfgTDk3lz1wr3Z0jFtftLt4pR9gWrn6au7B3PqJ.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/aDfgTDk3lz1wr3Z0jFtftLt4pR9gWrn6au7B3PqJ.png\"></p></li></ul>",
                'toc' => [['id' => "when-do-you-need-to-rebuild-annual-rollovers", 'text' => "When do you need to Rebuild Annual Rollovers?", 'level' => "H1"], ['id' => "how-to-rebuild-annual-rollovers", 'text' => "How to Rebuild Annual Rollovers?", 'level' => "H1"]],
                'is_active' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2026-04-09 17:47:51',
                'updated_at' => '2026-05-04 18:50:34',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 4,
                'title' => "Process - Breach Notices and Oncharges",
                'slug' => "process-breach-notices-and-oncharges",
                'content' => "<h1 id=\"breach-notice-misc-invoice-and-cqmf\"><strong>Breach notice</strong> (Misc Invoice and CQMF)</h1><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Lileth receives request from OCM/OCA</p></li><li><p>Lileth to</p><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>create a Misc Invoice (7 days from issue date which is today)</p></li><li><p>send to OCM/COA (not Cindy) within 24-48 hours.</p></li></ol></li><li><p>Lileth to process a CQMF for MOCS charge</p></li><li><p>Lileth’s email should specify <em>please send to the owner for payment</em>.</p></li></ol><hr><h1 id=\"oncharge\"><strong>Oncharge</strong></h1><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Lot owner oncharge (Levy Journal)</p><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Lileth receives request from OCM/OCA</p></li><li><p>For multi-OCs, check expense to ensure OC allocation is consistent. If not, check with OCM. If invoice not in detailed expense, process as per request</p></li><li><p>Lileth to</p><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>post Levy Journal (28 days from issue date which is today)</p></li><li><p>send to Cindy (not OCM/OCA) within 24-48 hours.</p></li></ol></li><li><p>Lileth’s email should</p><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>attach the invoice to be oncharged (watermarked DO NOT PAY)</p></li><li><p>request Cindy to send notice to OCM/OCA</p></li></ol></li></ol></li><li><p>Contractor oncharge (Misc Invoice)</p><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Lileth receives request from OCM/OCA</p></li><li><p>Lileth to create a Misc Invoice (7 days from issue date which is today) under dummy Lot 9999 and send to OCM/COA (not Cindy) within 24-48 hours</p></li><li><p> Lileth’s email should</p><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>attach the invoice to be oncharged (watermarked DO NOT PAY)</p></li><li><p>specify <em>please send to the contractor for payment</em></p></li></ol></li></ol></li></ol>",
                'toc' => [['id' => "breach-notice-misc-invoice-and-cqmf", 'text' => "Breach notice (Misc Invoice and CQMF)", 'level' => "H1"], ['id' => "oncharge", 'text' => "Oncharge", 'level' => "H1"]],
                'is_active' => 1,
                'created_at' => '2026-04-09 17:50:16',
                'updated_at' => '2026-05-04 18:45:54',
            ],
            [
                'id' => 5,
                'title' => "MOCS Process",
                'slug' => "mocs-process",
                'content' => "<h1 id=\"purpose\" ><strong>Purpose</strong></h1><p>This procedure outlines the steps for processing invoices to ensure accurate, timely, and efficient payment to vendors, and proper financial recordkeeping.​</p><hr><h1 id=\"roles-and-responsibilitiesu200b\" ><strong>Roles and Responsibilities</strong>​</h1><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Vendor/Supplier: Submits the invoice in the prescribed format.​</p></li><li><p>Invoicing Team - Reviews and processes invoices, ensuring accuracy.​</p></li><li><p>Managers - Authorize invoice approval.​</p></li><li><p>Payables Team - Payment processing</p></li></ol><hr><h1 id=\"invoice-receiptu200b\" ><strong>Invoice Receipt</strong>​</h1><p><strong>Step 1</strong>: Invoices are received via email.​</p><p><strong>Step 2</strong>: The invoicing team will upload the invoices to PIQ, either via Systool or through manual uploading.​</p><p><strong>Step 3</strong>: Tax Invoices should include the following details:​</p><ul><li><p>Vendor Name​</p></li><li><p>Invoice Date​</p></li><li><p>Invoice Number​</p></li><li><p>Work Order (WO) Number (if applicable)​</p></li><li><p>Description of services​</p></li><li><p>Total Amount Due​</p></li><li><p>Payment Details​</p></li></ul><hr><h1 id=\"invoice-review-and-verificationu200b\" ><strong>Invoice Review and Verification</strong>​</h1><p>The invoicing team needs to check the following:​</p><ul><li><p>​<strong>Tax Invoice Document </strong>– <em>Ensure the document is a valid tax invoice.</em>​</p></li><li><p><strong>Correctness of Supplier Information </strong>- <em>Ensure the supplier details match company records.</em>​</p></li><li><p>​<strong>Matching WO </strong>- <em>If a WO was issued, verify the WO number and details match the invoice.</em>​</p></li></ul><p>​Incomplete or incorrect invoices should be flagged and returned to the supplier for correction.​</p><hr><h1 id=\"invoice-processing-restrictionsu200b\" ><strong>Invoice Processing Restrictions</strong>​</h1><p>The following restrictions apply to the invoice processing procedure:​</p><ul><li><p><strong>Invoice Format Requirement - </strong><em>All invoices must be submitted in PDF format. If an invoice is received in a non-PDF format, it must be returned to the supplier with a request for  them to convert the invoice to PDF format and resubmit it.</em>​</p></li><li><p><strong>Invoice Submission Requirements </strong>– <em>Invoices that are incomplete or lack essential details (such as vendor name, SP number, Job Address or total amount) will not be processed and must be returned to the supplier for correction.</em>​</p></li><li><p><strong>Duplicate Invoices </strong>- <em>Any suspected duplicates will be flagged for investigation before processing.</em>​</p></li><li><p><strong>Overdue Utility Bills or Levy Notices - </strong>Current charges that are not overdue (i.e., the charges for the current billing cycle) can be processed for payment immediately, even if there are overdue amounts.</p></li><li><p><em>If an invoice reflects an overdue amount for utility bills (e.g., electricity, water, phone, gas) or a levy notice, do not process the overdue amount for payment and immediately forward the invoice to the @Payables team.</em></p></li></ul><hr><h1 id=\"invoice-processing-restrictionsu200b\" ><strong>Invoice Processing Restrictions</strong>​</h1><ul><li><p><strong>Telstra Bills </strong>– <em>When processing Telstra bills, ensure the full amount, including any out standing balance, is paid, as original invoices cannot be requested</em>​</p></li><li><p><strong>Duplicate Invoices </strong>- <em>Any suspected duplicates will be flagged for investigation before processing.</em>​</p></li><li><p><strong>Overdue Utility Bills or Levy Notices - </strong>Current charges that are not overdue (i.e., the charges for the current billing cycle) can be processed for payment immediately, even if there are overdue amounts.. ​</p></li><li><p><em>If an invoice reflects an overdue amount for utility bills (e.g. , electricity, water, phone, gas) or a levy notice, do not process the overdue amount for payment and immediately forward the invoice to the @Payables team</em></p><hr><h1 id=\"log-in-piqu200b\" ><strong>Log in PIQ</strong>​</h1><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Copy paste the link</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://mcdonald.propertyiq.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">https://mcdonald.propertyiq.com.au</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://southerncross.propertyiq.com.au\">https://southerncross.propertyiq.com.au</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://beaconocm.propertyiq.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">https://beaconocm.propertyiq.com.au</a></p></li></ul></li><li><p>Username : <a href=\"mailto:Ronale@mocs.com.au\" target=\"_blank\">Ronale@mocs.com.au</a> (Mcdonald)​</p></li></ol><p>Username : RonaleO (SCS &amp; BC)​</p><p>Password: Joggers1129$ (Mcdonald)​</p><p>Password: Ronale@2024 (SCS &amp; BC)​</p><ol start=\"3\"><li><p>Click Sign In​</p></li><li><p>Enter authentication code​</p></li><li><p>Click Sign In​</p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/OIcEWYntIJz6tdLgAEHQxbpSfyiYfTIZeD4YcrPb.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/OIcEWYntIJz6tdLgAEHQxbpSfyiYfTIZeD4YcrPb.png\"></p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/neJzj2pTlRTX2h5rTtWk1g6I286QGleTfaGxbjSG.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/neJzj2pTlRTX2h5rTtWk1g6I286QGleTfaGxbjSG.png\"></p><hr></li></ol></li></ul><h1 id=\"open-piq-system\" ><strong>Open PIQ System</strong></h1><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>When you first open PIQ. Select Processing &gt; Supplier Transaction​</p></li><li><p>This will direct you to the page displayed here, which contains all the uploaded invoices. ​</p></li></ol><p>While processing invoice ensure that the mode selected as <strong>Entry mode</strong> and select all folio drop down button to select that portfolio that you will be processing Ex: VJ RAY, City home. <strong>Use All Folio </strong>for now.​</p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/uPxduyQJtglrYjpvs6jpUX3yVrO6BxnBH8GeelMs.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/uPxduyQJtglrYjpvs6jpUX3yVrO6BxnBH8GeelMs.png\">\\\\\\\\</p><hr><h1 id=\"uploading-of-invoices-on-piqu00a0\" ><strong>Uploading of Invoices on PIQ </strong></h1><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Entry Mode must be selected for invoice processing​</p></li><li><p>Choose from the dropdown option which folio you would be processing. Please use <strong>all folio </strong>for now.<strong> </strong>​</p></li><li><p><strong>folios </strong>​</p></li><li><p>Upload Invoice can be used for quick uploading of any invoice for processing​</p></li><li><p>Once you select <strong>upload invoice</strong> a box will popup. You can simply drag the <strong>PDF file </strong>from the email and drop it inside the box.​</p></li><li><p>For <strong>Systool</strong>, you may check the manual how to upload bulk invoices from <strong>outlook</strong>.​</p></li></ol><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/NaTbsrXycXHCPccrsbyeUSLeOgnV4hxnMe2LVksI.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/NaTbsrXycXHCPccrsbyeUSLeOgnV4hxnMe2LVksI.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"processing-of-invoiceu200b\" ><strong>Processing of Invoice</strong>​</h1><p>Please follow the steps below to process the invoice. Kindly ensure to double check the information before proceeding.​</p><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Type Supplier Name – Click Scope​</p></li><li><p>Check BSB &amp; Account or BPAY biller code​</p></li><li><p>Type Plan number or search the address on the scope​</p></li><li><p>Input Work order number or Search – seepage 11.​</p></li><li><p>Type or Copy Paste Invoice/Ref number​</p></li><li><p> Type Amount​</p></li><li><p> Select Contribution Schedule​</p></li><li><p>Enter the details of what the invoice stated or Copy from Work Order – seepage 11 or13.​</p></li><li><p>Input the Expense Account – see page 12​</p></li><li><p>Click Pay Later​</p></li></ol><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/3UaZptArg5m3LpppqVkZGzL4tKvJVZcaIyJMfAdU.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/3UaZptArg5m3LpppqVkZGzL4tKvJVZcaIyJMfAdU.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"for-duplicateu00a0invoiceu200b\" ><strong>For Duplicate Invoice</strong>​</h1><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Go to <strong>Ledger</strong> icon.​</p></li><li><p>Type the details from the invoice.​</p><p>Ex. INV-0613 then <strong>Click Search</strong>​</p></li><li><p>Check if there is something similar on​ history.​</p></li><li><p>Please <strong>delete</strong> the invoice if it appears to be same in the history.​</p></li></ol><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/gQftN6E7KhO6rA51xh8uEA9YRk9aJMIbNzH1703N.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/gQftN6E7KhO6rA51xh8uEA9YRk9aJMIbNzH1703N.png\"></p><h3 id=\"important-u2013-only-process-tax-invoicesu00a0u200b\" ><strong><span data-color=\"red\" class=\"color\" style=\"--color: oklch(0.577 0.245 27.325); --dark-color: oklch(0.704 0.191 22.216)\">Important – Only Process Tax Invoices </span></strong><span data-color=\"red\" class=\"color\" style=\"--color: oklch(0.577 0.245 27.325); --dark-color: oklch(0.704 0.191 22.216)\">​</span></h3><p>​Once all the details are entered click on Pay Later at the bottom right.​</p><p>​<strong>Before Clicking Pay Later make sure all the details are correct</strong></p><p></p><p>Important note:​</p><ul><li><p> Please process only <strong>tax invoice</strong>.​</p></li><li><p><strong>Do not process any overdue/reminder notice from utility and any statement from supplier</strong>. You can send these to payables (<em>payables@mocs.com.au</em>) so that the original bill can be requested or investigate why this happened.​</p></li></ul><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/8VVYDNk8hA8HGZe35mR0Ju9sOzd4rOX9YbK4jx5K.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/8VVYDNk8hA8HGZe35mR0Ju9sOzd4rOX9YbK4jx5K.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"additional-guidelinesu00a0u200b\" ><strong>Additional Guidelines </strong>​</h1><ul><li><p><strong>Creditor:</strong>​ You can enter all the details as per the invoice. You can use the little scope which will list all the suppliers to search for the supplier.​ Only Supplier Code can be entered here directly. ​</p></li></ul><p><strong>For Ex</strong>: MJS. If not sure on the code click the scope button and look up by supplier name. ​</p><p>The same goes for all other details.​</p><p>Always check for the Creditors <strong>ABN, BSB &amp; Account number</strong>, it should match the ABN, BSB &amp; Account number in the system and with the document on your workflow.​</p><p>​</p><ul><li><p><strong>If No Creditor’s name:</strong>​ You may locate the Creditor’s name by the steps on the page 8 .​</p></li></ul><p>​</p><ul><li><p><strong>Plan Number:</strong>​ Sometimes Plan number is not visible, you may locate the Strata plan number by the steps on the page 9.​</p></li></ul><p>​</p><ul><li><p><strong>Work Order:</strong>​ If there is Work number on the invoice, please enter in the system.​</p></li></ul><p>The Details, it should match what is entered into Work Order. Seepage 10.​</p><p>​</p><ul><li><p><strong>Reference Number:</strong>​ While entering the reference number (Tax invoice number), if you receive duplicate warning check on the ledger and delete if same. ​</p></li></ul><p>See <a href=\"http://jatrobpo-chatbot-v2.test/knowledge-base?document=14#important-only-process-tax-invoices\">page 13</a> for an example.​</p><p>​</p><ul><li><p><strong>Details:</strong>​ Always put the Unit Number. Double check the details before Click Pay Later.​</p></li></ul><p>​</p><ul><li><p><strong>Account Expense</strong>:​ See page 11.​</p></li></ul><p>If you are not sure which expense account you will enter, you can view the ledger.​</p><hr><h1 id=\"how-to-search-suppliercreditoru2019s-nameu00a0u200b\" ><strong>How to Search Supplier/Creditor’s Name </strong>​</h1><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Click File (Supplier)​</p></li><li><p>Select All​</p></li><li><p>Type the ABN​</p></li><li><p>Check for the Creditors ABN Number, It should match the ABN in the system and with the document on your workflow.​</p></li><li><p>If the Creditor is inactive or non-compliant email compliance team.(suppliers@mocs.com.au)</p></li></ol><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/YitZp3q3eSvcw9Z9OdADYZKEl53jBCi3PWfYS5eI.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/YitZp3q3eSvcw9Z9OdADYZKEl53jBCi3PWfYS5eI.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"how-to-locate-sp-numberu200b\" ><strong>How to locate SP Number?</strong>​</h1><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Click Scope​</p></li><li><p>Type-In the Street address (Example: Barkly Place). The system will show all related address from this street.​</p></li><li><p>Choose the specific address and click. (The Strata Plan number should appear automatically).​</p></li></ol><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/Vy9WwEo18z3OTqNQb0dGcVemyL0AcUi4lsOuFDo6.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/Vy9WwEo18z3OTqNQb0dGcVemyL0AcUi4lsOuFDo6.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"work-orderu200b\" ><strong>Work Order</strong>​</h1><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>If there is <strong>Work order number </strong>on the invoice, please enter in the system.​</p></li><li><p>You can also click on the scope to view <strong>Workorder</strong> and <strong>Select</strong> the one for the invoice.​</p></li><li><p>You can untick all tabs Except <strong>In Progress </strong>to view just the open ones and <strong>select the correct one. </strong>(Unticking will filter out as below).​</p></li><li><p> Please ensure WO number is entered if shown in invoice so that the WO can be closed.</p></li><li><p>Then Select but make sure that the Work Order matches the work done t the property​</p></li></ol><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/0G3EEJfxZlp2rYxIt4ZqOXeL56FI4wz2svE3LHop.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/0G3EEJfxZlp2rYxIt4ZqOXeL56FI4wz2svE3LHop.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"expense-account-guidelines\" ><strong>Expense Account Guidelines</strong></h1><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Select the most appropriate account from the list.​</p></li><li><p>Once you&#039;re familiar with the account codes, you can enter the code directly into the box.</p><p><strong><em>Note</em></strong><em>: A red highlight indicates that the expense account is not budgeted for the Strata Plan.</em></p></li></ol><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/jl7Ojezqfem1tTS0NaCSSWhfG7pW6qX75A0P0wqm.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/jl7Ojezqfem1tTS0NaCSSWhfG7pW6qX75A0P0wqm.png\"></p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/nXm5K8scRB0fEE2pVhzRzXB862hY99QMmgT69YXC.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/nXm5K8scRB0fEE2pVhzRzXB862hY99QMmgT69YXC.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"descriptiondetails\" ><strong>Description/Details</strong></h1><p>If the work order is not available, you can enter the information from the invoice or check the ledger for the description used.​ Steps to Check the Ledger:​</p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/uvp8O0sQfYFieStlHT1xcTT8x74njWY7CCy5IY8v.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/uvp8O0sQfYFieStlHT1xcTT8x74njWY7CCy5IY8v.png\"></p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/jnkbuiKRjzmIhruEvtK7u54vrMqIBHpStwFOGzSV.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/jnkbuiKRjzmIhruEvtK7u54vrMqIBHpStwFOGzSV.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"guidelines-for-utility-billsu200b\" ><strong>Guidelines for Utility Bills:</strong>​</h1><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>If there is a Credit Note (or an invoice with a credit amount), forward it to Payable for investigation.​</p></li><li><p>Input the Supplier Name.​</p></li><li><p>CRN Number: Enter without spaces.​</p></li><li><p>Reference Number: Enter the full invoice number with no spaces. For bills like Utility Sydney Water and Energy Australia, which don’t have an invoice number, enter &quot;SP&quot; followed by the last date of the billing period. <strong>Example</strong>: The SP number ois SP22166 and the billing period was 26 Oct 22 – 23 Jan 23 <span data-color=\"red\" class=\"color\" style=\"--color: oklch(0.577 0.245 27.325); --dark-color: oklch(0.704 0.191 22.216)\">SP</span>+<span data-color=\"blue\" class=\"color\" style=\"--color: oklch(0.546 0.245 262.881); --dark-color: oklch(0.707 0.165 254.624)\">ddmmyyyy </span>=<span data-color=\"red\" class=\"color\" style=\"--color: oklch(0.577 0.245 27.325); --dark-color: oklch(0.704 0.191 22.216)\">22166</span><span data-color=\"blue\" class=\"color\" style=\"--color: oklch(0.546 0.245 262.881); --dark-color: oklch(0.707 0.165 254.624)\">23012023​</span></p></li><li><p> Check the BPAY Biller Code.​</p></li><li><p>Description: Enter the billing period as shown on the invoice (e.g., Water 28/10/22 – 23/1/23).​</p></li><li><p>Expense Account: Select based on the utility type—Water, Electricity, or Gas.</p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/Hy50OuYArvoFCPqm0FNKYRq5KviERFuxYhYwNQOk.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/Hy50OuYArvoFCPqm0FNKYRq5KviERFuxYhYwNQOk.png\"> ​</p><hr><h1 id=\"guidelines-for-utility-bills-with-balance-carried-forward-u200b\" ><strong>Guidelines for Utility Bills with Balance Carried Forward </strong>​</h1><p>For Sydney Water bills, if the balance is less than $50 and there is a previous payment. Process the invoice as shown in the image. If the balance is more the $50 see instruction below.​</p><p>​For utility bills with an outstanding balance, Process the current charge, and email <a href=\"mailto:payables@mocs.com.au\" target=\"_blank\">payables@mocs.com.au</a> to request the original bills for the outstanding amount. ​</p></li></ol><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/rcg5TRy2gVWkOyQ1rpljQsC4EPLCfisYsqkwwefl.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/rcg5TRy2gVWkOyQ1rpljQsC4EPLCfisYsqkwwefl.png\"></p><p><strong>Note: ​</strong></p><ul><li><p>Do not process utility bills with amounts less that $1. Send to <a href=\"mailto:payables@mocs.com.au\">payables@mocs.com.au</a> ​</p></li><li><p>Send the emails for invoices with outstanding balances for electricity and water bills separately.​</p></li></ul><hr><h1 id=\"telstra-process\" ><strong>Telstra Process</strong></h1><p>​​Process the whole amount including the outstanding balance.</p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/leHVEu9J8aDgQ8wPZgyJb7VKKhm7XJYUP7pK9yH5.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/leHVEu9J8aDgQ8wPZgyJb7VKKhm7XJYUP7pK9yH5.png\"></p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/XnSESgafvndwgFoAKSUZ8F7tyiT65qsqIDx5yU7y.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/XnSESgafvndwgFoAKSUZ8F7tyiT65qsqIDx5yU7y.png\"></p><p><strong>Note</strong>​</p><ul><li><p>If there is a Credit note (or an invoice with a Credit amount) in the queue, forward to Payables (<a href=\"mailto:payables@mocs.com.au\"><em>payables@mocs.com.au</em></a>) for investigation.​</p></li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Note: For Invoices from Remond is Check the SP </strong>​</p><p><strong>Number on the System vs on the Invoice.</strong>​</p><p><strong><em>Reminder</em></strong></p><ul><li><p>his Supplier have<strong> different bank account for different Strata Plans</strong>. ​</p></li><li><p>Double check the Bank Details in the invoice in system. When you select a supplier, it will show the bank details on the right side. ​</p></li><li><p>Please ensure the correct bank account is selected for the invoice.​</p></li></ul><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/SpjoYlZwvOCpsoDBZ9tajpBlfiwnlkd8hH61QJQk.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/SpjoYlZwvOCpsoDBZ9tajpBlfiwnlkd8hH61QJQk.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"direct-debitu200b\" ><strong>Direct Debit</strong>​</h1><p><strong>Direct Debit invoices </strong>– do not process send to Payables(<em>payables@mocs.com.aum</em>)​</p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/qmvB8GI4zRrefIuaJPGQcnuK6KXP05smZVkCveOb.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/qmvB8GI4zRrefIuaJPGQcnuK6KXP05smZVkCveOb.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"processing-levy-contributions-invoicesu200b\" ><strong>Processing Levy Contributions Invoices</strong>​</h1><p>This is similar to Utility bills, <strong>only the current period amount</strong> should be entered on Levy notices.</p><p></p><p><strong><em>Note: </em></strong>Do not include the Arrears amount.</p><p>Send to <a href=\"mailto:payables@mocs.com.au\"><u>payables@mocs.com.au</u></a> in case there is an Arrears amount</p><p></p><p><em>Please see image for an example:</em></p><p>The amount should be entered for this one is $4,673.81.</p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/1kUovfndqF6fjY3Z4jnMwmleOphgV4oVnwlvrzep.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/1kUovfndqF6fjY3Z4jnMwmleOphgV4oVnwlvrzep.png\"></p><hr><ul><li><p>If the <strong>Payee hasn&#039;t been set up as a supplier</strong> in the system, forward the Reimbursement form to <a href=\"mailto:creditors@mocs.com.au\">creditors@mocs.com.au</a> for set up.​</p></li><li><p>If the form is missing manager&#039;s signature or supporting document, send it back to the manager.​</p></li><li><p>The amount on the request should match the amount on the supporting documents.</p><p>For <strong>reimbursement Reference number </strong>:​ <span data-color=\"red\" class=\"color\" style=\"--color: oklch(0.577 0.245 27.325); --dark-color: oklch(0.704 0.191 22.216)\">SP NUMBER</span>+<span data-color=\"green\" class=\"color\" style=\"--color: oklch(0.627 0.194 149.214); --dark-color: oklch(0.792 0.209 151.711)\">REIMB</span>+<span data-color=\"blue\" class=\"color\" style=\"--color: oklch(0.546 0.245 262.881); --dark-color: oklch(0.707 0.165 254.624)\">Request Date</span></p></li></ul><p><em>Ex: <span data-color=\"red\" class=\"color\" style=\"--color: oklch(0.577 0.245 27.325); --dark-color: oklch(0.704 0.191 22.216)\">270827</span><span data-color=\"green\" class=\"color\" style=\"--color: oklch(0.627 0.194 149.214); --dark-color: oklch(0.792 0.209 151.711)\">REIMB</span><span data-color=\"blue\" class=\"color\" style=\"--color: oklch(0.546 0.245 262.881); --dark-color: oklch(0.707 0.165 254.624)\">21022024</span></em></p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/63WMZHNEuFqsZIGReeBt5sNcfCDh5GNvCL8XDpJk.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/63WMZHNEuFqsZIGReeBt5sNcfCDh5GNvCL8XDpJk.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"insurance-invoicesu200b\" ><strong>Insurance Invoices</strong>​</h1><p></p><ul><li><p>Always check if it is an insurance renewal,transfer, or endorsement invoice.​</p></li><li><p>Description: Type of Insurance + Period Coverage ​</p><p>Sample: <strong>Transfer Renewal 31/3/24 – 31/3/25</strong></p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/eK64D8KCAyyHHiyVHuV050mg9uaQ9NAmTz6xdNxB.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/eK64D8KCAyyHHiyVHuV050mg9uaQ9NAmTz6xdNxB.png\">​</p></li></ul><p><em>See next slide for the steps on how to split Insurance Invoice</em>.</p><hr><h1 id=\"split-insurance-invoicesu200b\" ><strong>Split Insurance Invoices</strong>​</h1><p>A <strong>GST amount </strong>should be shown on the <strong>PIQ System </strong>to determine if the invoice should be <strong>split</strong>. If the GST amount is zero, process it usual.​</p><ul><li><p>the <strong>First Column </strong>the amount would be: <strong>Total Amount– Stamp Duty </strong>(stamp duty on the invoice)​</p></li><li><p>​For the <strong>Second Column </strong>just input the <strong>Stamp Duty </strong>Amount from the <strong>Invoice</strong>. The then <strong>change the GST</strong> to <strong>Free</strong>​</p></li><li><p>​Description of the Second column:​</p></li><li><p>Type of Insurance + Period Coverage + (Stamp Duty)​</p></li><li><p><strong><em>Sample</em></strong><em>: Insurance Renewal 31/3/24 – 31/3/25 (Stamp Duty)</em></p></li><li><p>Add all the <strong>GST from the Invoice</strong> then see if it <strong>match</strong> with the <strong>GST on PIQ System</strong>. ​​</p></li></ul><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/9hkvpp1xfEDggdiw3PVNzrS3ILUkRCSeSZstVUWi.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/9hkvpp1xfEDggdiw3PVNzrS3ILUkRCSeSZstVUWi.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"insurance-quotesu200b\" ><strong>Insurance Quotes</strong>​</h1><ul><li><p>Proceed with processing for the suppliers <strong>CHU Underwriting Agencies </strong>and <strong>Strata Community Insurance Agencies</strong>, as they only provide quotes​</p></li><li><p>Use the policy/quote number as reference number.​</p></li></ul><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/R93ka333gtExz1AN0QdBQuSto2QIXi0Wcw8vuM9U.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/R93ka333gtExz1AN0QdBQuSto2QIXi0Wcw8vuM9U.png\"></p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/1c8B41F96GOQm5Sa8goowHflvgsZhpr1N4eNHQo0.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/1c8B41F96GOQm5Sa8goowHflvgsZhpr1N4eNHQo0.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"collection-invoicesu200b\" ><strong>Collection Invoices</strong>​</h1><ul><li><p>​Check for <strong>Lot #</strong> on the invoice to determine if it is a <strong>collection invoice</strong>. ForChambers Russell invoice​</p></li><li><p>Details Format - Lot # - (the action as per the invoice) – (supplier) INV(invoice number)”​</p></li><li><p><em>Sample: <strong>Lot 2 – Levy Recovery Proceedings – Chambers Russell: INVB25095</strong></em>​</p></li><li><p><strong><em>Use A4LEGALDR </em></strong>expense account for <strong>mcdonald</strong>​</p></li><li><p>Use <strong><em>A4LEGALDR</em></strong> for expense account for <strong>beacon</strong>​</p></li><li><p>Use <strong>A4MANDEBT</strong> expense account for <strong>southern cross</strong></p></li><li><p>Additional Steps (<em>after the usual process</em>)​</p></li><li><p>Click <strong>Charge Owner</strong>.​</p></li><li><p>Enter the <strong>Due Date </strong>same as the <strong>Notice Date.</strong>​</p></li><li><p>For the details, Just <strong>copy the details above</strong>.​</p></li><li><p><strong>Admin Account </strong>is same as the expense account.​</p></li><li><p>Tick the <strong>Generate Special Levy Notice</strong> and <strong>Include Copy of Invoice </strong>boxes.​</p></li><li><p>Click the <strong>add lot allocation</strong>. ​</p></li><li><p>Search the <strong>lot number</strong>.​</p></li><li><p>Enter the <strong>amount</strong>.​</p></li></ul><p><strong>Note: Collection invoices are not editable so make sure to double check the details before clicking pay later. If you accidentally process incorrect details, and if it is for deletion, please notify Amanda and Jingjing as well.</strong>​</p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/72uBxjEH4W0JOaAxDPvOBSvL9IVIvDOXY1iPwLBp.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/72uBxjEH4W0JOaAxDPvOBSvL9IVIvDOXY1iPwLBp.png\"></p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/qxnYFRt6DKLRMou3pefprk4rFBUUYh6qVtkJPIN0.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/qxnYFRt6DKLRMou3pefprk4rFBUUYh6qVtkJPIN0.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"reimbursement-strata-hub-receipt-nsw-government-u200b\" ><strong>Reimbursement: Strata Hub Receipt (<em>NSW Government</em>) </strong>​</h1><ul><li><p>Enter the S/Plan Number first​</p></li><li><p>Check the folio of the S/Plan by clicking the view button beside the plan number.​</p></li><li><p>Search REIMB on the supplier scope, then select the supplier based on the folio​</p></li><li><p>Make sure it’s <strong>GST Free </strong>before clicking Pay Later ​</p></li></ul><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/i0mGMmZ1J6NL6rwFxMLTtMW6AXDrGyUj9nNJs1pu.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/i0mGMmZ1J6NL6rwFxMLTtMW6AXDrGyUj9nNJs1pu.png\"></p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/4DSh2FH4J1aRvGpiaH9uJUSN44WYYOvZX8HY15Ms.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/4DSh2FH4J1aRvGpiaH9uJUSN44WYYOvZX8HY15Ms.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"bpay-payment-strata-hub-receipt-nsw-government\" ><strong>BPAY Payment: Strata Hub Receipt (<em>NSW Government</em>)</strong></h1><ul><li><p>The admin team will send through a PDF print out of an email received from Service NSW looking like the image on the side.​</p></li><li><p>Use supplier Service NSW with the biller code (247353) and CRN showing in the document.​</p></li><li><p>The SP number is shown in the reference.​</p></li><li><p>Enter the amount and use the expense code A4HUB.​</p></li></ul><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/3qcFmszLQu1uwMG0THFttvOCp9gjS3AjBN9sGJv9.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/3qcFmszLQu1uwMG0THFttvOCp9gjS3AjBN9sGJv9.png\"></p><p><img src=\"/storage/knowledge-base-images/WDIdUfHTfbDI6MQ3GsVT9OplTBKzFi42qqLw1kvH.png\" data-id=\"knowledge-base-images/WDIdUfHTfbDI6MQ3GsVT9OplTBKzFi42qqLw1kvH.png\"></p><hr><h1 id=\"v-j-ray-valuations-pty-ltdu200b\" ><strong>V J Ray (Valuations) Pty Ltd</strong>​</h1><ul><li><p><strong>Procedure: Handling Duplicate Valuation Invoices</strong>​</p></li><li><p>​If the second valuation invoice amount differs from the first one paid, please email <a href=\"mailto:jingjing@mocs.com.au\">jingjing@mocs.com.au</a> for review.​</p></li><li><p>If both invoices are for the same amount, do not process the invoice. Instead, send it to Payables for filing.​</p></li></ul><hr><h1 id=\"emailsu200b\" ><strong>Emails</strong>​</h1><ul><li><p><strong>Compliance Team - </strong><a href=\"mailto:suppliers@mocs.com.au\">suppliers@mocs.com.au</a>​</p></li><li><p>Inactive​</p></li><li><p>Non-compliant suppliers.​</p></li><li><p><strong>Creditors – </strong><a href=\"mailto:creditors@mocs.com.au\">creditors@mocs.com.au</a>​</p></li><li><p>Different bank details/ABN​</p></li><li><p>New Supplier (Can&#039;t Locate the Supplier in the System)​</p></li><li><p>Setting up of Owner for Reimbursement, Professionals, Insurance Brokers, and City Councils, Utility Providers​</p><p><em>These types of suppliers do not need compliance check.</em>​</p></li><li><p>Insurance Broker/Company​</p></li><li><p>Professionals (accountant, legal firm, property manager, etc.) ​</p></li><li><p>Public sector creditor (city council, revenue office, taxation office, etc.)​</p></li><li><p><strong>Contractor/Supplier/Creditor </strong>​</p></li><li><p>has Two SP on the invoice​</p></li><li><p>Building cannot be identified or building number and address are not consistent.​</p></li><li><p><strong>Payables – </strong><a href=\"mailto:payables@mocs.com.au\">payables@mocs.com.au</a>​</p></li><li><p>Duplicate invoice number​</p></li><li><p>Credit bills​</p></li><li><p>Lost Plan​</p></li><li><p>Outstanding Balance on Utility Bills and Arrears on Levies ​</p></li><li><p>Discrepancy amounts​</p></li><li><p>Overdue Reminders​</p></li><li><p>Cheque Payment​</p></li><li><p>Delete invoice​</p></li><li><p>Remittance Advice​</p></li><li><p>If a supplier is once-off type and is non-compliant​</p></li><li><p>and others concern/assistance​</p></li><li><p><strong>Managers</strong>​</p></li><li><p>For Victorian Buildings allocation (PS602491, PS704855Q &amp; PS504176C)​</p></li><li><p>Bills – SP and Supply address does not match​</p></li><li><p><strong>Amanda</strong>​</p></li><li><p>Incorrect input – Deletion of Collection invoices​</p></li><li><p><strong>Anjalee</strong>​</p></li><li><p>2022 Invoices ​</p></li></ul><hr><h1 id=\"detailed-email-instructions\" ><strong>Detailed Email Instructions</strong></h1><ul><li><p><strong>Handling Overdue Amounts on Utility Bills and Levy Notices</strong>​</p></li><li><p>If an overdue amount on any utility bill (e.g., electricity, water, phone, gas) or on a levy notice from a DP, do not process the overdue amount. Instead, forward the invoice to @Payables, so that the payables team can investigate and request the overdue invoices for processing. ​</p></li><li><p>Please ensure that you <strong>send separate emails for each type of utility bill with an outstanding balance</strong>. <strong>One email should be sent for water bills</strong>, another for <strong>electricity bills</strong>, and a separate one for <strong>phone bills.</strong>​</p></li><li><p>• <strong>Handling Non-PDF Invoices</strong>​</p></li><li><p>If an invoice is received in a format other than PDF, please request the sender to convert the invoice to PDF format and resend it to <a href=\"mailto:invoices@mocs.com.au\">invoices@mocs.com.au</a>.​</p></li><li><p>The supplier sends the original invoice as a PDF attachment. Any <strong>reminder emails are sent as links</strong> and <strong>can be safely ignored</strong>.​</p></li><li><p><strong>Procedure: One-Off Supplier Invoices that are Non-Compliant</strong>​</p></li><li><p>If an invoice is received in a format other than PDF, please request the sender to convert the invoice to PDF format and resend it to <a href=\"mailto:invoices@mocs.com.au\">invoices@mocs.com.au</a>.​</p></li><li><p><strong>Procedure: Identifying Lot Owners Providing Services</strong>​</p></li><li><p>If you come across an invoice where the <strong>supplier is a lot owner </strong>and no ABN is listed, <strong>please forward a copy of the invoice to <a href=\"mailto:suppliers@mocs.com.au\">suppliers@mocs.com.au</a></strong>​</p></li><li><p><strong>Procedure: Processing Older Integrity Invoices</strong>​</p></li><li><p>If you receive any <strong>invoice older than 07/02/2025 </strong>for Integrity, please <strong>send it to Lyka </strong>to check in Strata Master. Once she confirms that the invoice has not been paid in Strata Master, you may proceed with processing the invoice.​</p></li><li><p><strong>Procedure: Invoices for SP77052</strong>​</p></li><li><p>All invoices for <strong>SP77052</strong> should be sent to <a href=\"mailto:fayez_j2000@yahoo.com.au\">fayez_j2000@yahoo.com.au</a> for review and approval, <strong>except for cleaning invoices</strong>.​\\\\\\\\</p></li></ul><hr><h1 id=\"outlook-folders\" ><strong>Outlook Folders</strong></h1><ul><li><p><strong>Ronale Folder </strong>​</p></li><li><p><strong>Inbox</strong> – Important Queries/Insurance Invoices​</p></li><li><p><strong>Insurance</strong> – Uploaded and Processed Insurance Invoices / Anything Related to Insurance​</p></li><li><p><strong>ZZ Important </strong>– Important Instructions and Emails​</p></li><li><p><strong>ZZ CC Only </strong>– Email that we are copied/not directly for us​</p></li><li><p><strong>ZZ Complete </strong>– Completed tasks/queries​</p></li><li><p><strong>ZZ Disregard Invoice/ Email </strong>– Unimportant Emails ​</p></li><li><p><strong>ZZ For Process </strong>– Pending Invoices to process ​</p></li><li><p>​<strong>Invoices Folder </strong>​</p></li><li><p><strong>Inbox</strong> – Where we receive most of the invoices​</p></li><li><p><strong>Bills</strong> – Utility Bills​</p></li><li><p><strong>Multiple Attachments </strong>– Emails with multiple attachments that will be manually uploaded to PIQ.​</p></li><li><p><strong>No Invoice Attached </strong>– Emails that has no invoice attached​</p></li><li><p><strong>To Upload </strong>– Invoices that will be uploaded to PIQ via Sys tool ​</p></li><li><p><strong>ZZ For Checking </strong>– Invoices that needs investigation​</p></li><li><p><strong>ZZ Overdue Reminder </strong>– Emails with Overdue Invoices ​</p></li><li><p><strong>ZZZ No PDF Attached </strong>– Other file type attached invoices such asWord/Excel/JPG​</p></li><li><p>​ <strong>Invoices – BC </strong>​</p></li><li><p><strong>Inbox</strong> – Invoices for Beacon​</p></li><li><p>​<strong>Invoices – SCS </strong>​</p></li><li><p><strong>Inbox</strong> – Invoices for Southern Cross ​</p></li></ul>",
